  "id": "Compound::DB00780 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Phenelzine, a monoamine oxidase inhibitor, is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through a series of binding interactions involving Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, all of which converge on the enzyme Cyp2c8 as a downstream target. The shared binding of Phenelzine to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, followed by the binding of Rifapentine or Ritonavir or Amiodarone, suggests a mechanism where Phenelzine indirectly influences Cyp2c8 through the modulation of its substrate-binding partners. The recurring role of organic amino compounds and the presence of enzyme inhibitors in the pathways highlight a potential regulatory mechanism involving the interaction of Phenelzine with cytochrome P450 enzymes. The integration of these pathways underscores a possible dependency on the metabolic activity of Cyp2c8, which is further supported by the presence of multiple binding interactions that suggest a complex, context-dependent relationship between Phenelzine and Cyp2c8.",
